"scaruffi":null},{"id":192934750972716,"name":"1001 Albums You Must Hear Before You Die","src":"charts","grp":"1001 Albums","list_year":null,"rank":729,"year":1992,"note":null,"total":999,"scaruffi":null}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"A new vinyl release of *Dirt* was remastered from the original audio, and due to the album's production era and likely studio practices, it is suggested that it could be a full end-to-end analog production, recorded on analog tape. This particular edition is split across two heavy vinyl discs, with three songs on each of the four sides, and is played at 33 RPM. \"This is dirt from Allison Chains. I see that it was remastered from the original audio.\"","year":1992,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"More Vinyl Stories","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B2g4QSREzpw"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"Alice in Chains' second album, *Dirt*, released in 1992, represented a full pivot to their grunge sound and image, having evolved from their earlier hair metal style. Given the album's dark themes, photographer Rocky Schenk aimed for a \"hellish\" and disturbing cover. The artwork features a nude woman, Mariah O'Brien, half-buried in what appears to be a cracked, dry desert floor, leaving her fate ambiguous. Layne Staley revealed his input for the cover was inspired by \"a certain person who basically buried my ass so the woman on the cover is kind of the portrayal of that person getting sucked down into the dirt instead of me.\" The \"desert\" was actually a set built in Schenk's Hollywood studio using miniatures for mountains and foam core/clay for the ground. \"So what we have is a cover featuring a nude woman half-barried in what looks like a cracked and dry desert floor.\"","year":1992,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The Stories Behind Iconic Album Covers Part 1","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sn5TWBFd0XM"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"This album set a high standard for Alice in Chains, with some later releases being perceived as not meeting the quality established by \"Dirt.\" \"up to the standards set by dirt a few years earlier.\"","year":1992,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Death as a Career Move ｜ From the Archives","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CTZ4FfDVFfE"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Grunge Album","body":"Released in 1992, \"Dirt\" by Alice in Chains is referenced as a quintessential example of the prevailing grunge sound of the early 90s. This album, characterized by \"guitarras tan duras tan garajeras\" (hard, garage-like guitars), provides crucial context for the musical landscape that Jeff Buckley, with his more intimate style, found challenging to navigate. \"el son y lluz es el dirte es de 1992.\"","year":1992,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"Recordando a Jeff Buckley","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aYB4LJSFwEo"}]}],"book_tracks":[{"id":276842043113536,"artist":"Alice In Chains","artist_id":34857375835151,"title":"Dirt","year":1992,"ess":0,"yt":"19CXYQhqVu0","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Grunge","scene_id":32992220995517,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#grunge","chapters":["Sección 6.12"],"pages":[[1,274,null]]}],"others":[{"id":92724788352542,"type":"album","name":"Facelift","year":1990,"weight":25},{"id":47900505581818,"type":"album","name":"Alice in Chains","year":1995,"weight":15},{"id":6527152130107,"type":"album","name":"Black Gives Way to Blue","year":2009,"weight":15},{"id":15795449790214,"type":"song","name":"Man in the Box","year":1991,"weight":10},{"id":132338082148590,"type":"song","name":"Sea of Sorrow","year":1990,"weight":7},{"id":134247646159401,"type":"album","name":"Jar of Flies","year":1994,"weight":6},{"id":113144919495495,"type":"song","name":"Grind","year":1995,"weight":6},{"id":231888117945095,"type":"album","name":"Unplugged","year":1996,"weight":4},{"id":177329919452575,"type":"song","name":"I Stay Away","year":null,"weight":4},{"id":162295873722682,"type":"album","name":"First Album (Early 1990s)","year":null,"weight":4},{"id":160503864414055,"type":"album","name":"Albums Released in 2010s","year":null,"weight":4},{"id":108247916154643,"type":"album","name":"Music Bank","year":1999,"weight":4}]}